<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zubayrids</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zubayrid</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zubayrids were the supporters of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-allah-ibn-al-zubayr">Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr</a>, who claimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-fitna">Second Fitna</a> after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazid-i">Yazid I</a> in 683. For several years they controlled much of the Islamic world. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> profile records that the Marwanid branch of the Umayyads recovered the caliphate from the Zubayrid claimants under Abd al-Malik, whose forces took Mecca in 692.</p></div>
